8
00:00:29.287 --> 00:00:30.161
Part 2.

9
00:00:30.441 --> 00:00:31.359
Key idea.

10
00:00:32.609 --> 00:00:36.107
A Count-Min Sketch is a d times w grid of counters.

11
00:00:36.387 --> 00:00:41.422
Each item increments one counter per row; the estimate is the minimum across rows.

12
00:00:41.702 --> 00:00:53.307
It never underestimates, and overestimates by at most ε, N with probability 1 minus δ (w = e or ε, d = ln(1 or δ)).

13
00:00:53.587 --> 00:01:00.691
Pair it with a size-K candidate set: after each update, an item enters if its estimate beats the weakest member.

14
00:01:02.041 --> 00:01:03.385
Here is the diagram.

